## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/defocus.html
- Summary (EN): Blurs an input layer the way a real camera lens does, with optional colour correction of out-of-focus areas and a custom bokeh mask.
- Résumé (FR) : Floute une image comme un objectif photographique à partir d'une carte de profondeur en mètres, avec une forme de bokeh personnalisable.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to defocus", "depth: depth map in meters giving each object's distance from the camera", "bokeh: optional mono mask shaping the blur; a circular bokeh is used if omitted", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Focus Distance: distance at which objects are sharp", "Focal Length: camera zoom to mimic", "F-Stop: strength of the defocus", "Focus Plane Blur: softens the transition between sharp and blurred areas", "Radius: maximum bokeh radius in pixels", "Gain: overall bokeh luminance", "Resample Input and Resolution: quality versus speed", "Color Correct group: brightness, saturation and gamma applied only to out-of-focus areas", "Depth Blend Min and Max: remap the depth range used to blend sharp and defocused layers"]

- Caveats: ["Large Radius values are expensive because many samples are scattered.", "Depth must be in meters for correct results.", "Resampling speeds up computation at a small quality cost.", "Karma can output a depth AOV for use with this node."]

